1
00:00:04,579 --> 00:00:06,789
Did you see the new budget memo
this morning?

2
00:00:06,956 --> 00:00:08,336
(Leonard:)Yeah, more cutbacks.

3
00:00:08,499 --> 00:00:10,839
(Sheldon:)Unacceptable. It baffles me...

4
00:00:11,002 --> 00:00:15,382
(Sheldon:)...why they don't simply let some of you go
so there's money available for my research.

5
00:00:16,883 --> 00:00:18,633
(Leonard:)You know what baffles me, Sheldon?

6
00:00:18,801 --> 00:00:22,261
(Sheldon:)Based on your academic record,
any number of things, I would imagine.

7
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:24,510
LESLIE: Hey, guys.
- Hi, Leslie.

8
00:00:24,682 --> 00:00:27,022
(Leslie:)I got the approval
for the rapid prototyper.

9
00:00:27,185 --> 00:00:29,225
(Howard:)That's great, Leslie. Thanks.

10
00:00:29,395 --> 00:00:31,485
(Leslie:)You scratch my back, I scratch yours.

11
00:00:31,648 --> 00:00:32,728
[GROWLS]

12
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,610
(Raj:)What was all that about?

13
00:00:37,111 --> 00:00:38,401
(Howard:)Oh, uh, no big deal.

14
00:00:38,571 --> 00:00:41,571
(Howard:)They gave Leslie control
over some unrestricted grant money.

15
00:00:41,741 --> 00:00:46,661
(Leonard:)Yeah, okay, but what's with
the back scratching and the meow?

16
00:00:47,288 --> 00:00:51,248
(Sheldon:)I believe the back-scratching metaphor
describes a quid pro quo situation...

17
00:00:51,417 --> 00:00:54,127
...where one party provides services
to the second party...

18
00:00:54,295 --> 00:00:57,715
(Sheldon:)- ...in compensation for a similar action.
- Thank you.

19
00:00:57,882 --> 00:01:03,022
The meow, that sounded to me
like an African civet cat.

